00:52:34,767 --> 00:52:36,700
Got it, hit 'em, trust me,

1302
00:52:36,733 --> 00:52:37,967
I got him right
between the eyes.

1303
00:52:38,000 --> 00:52:40,100
You can't see it, but I did.

1304
00:52:40,133 --> 00:52:41,433
Ah no, I'm still alive!

1305
00:52:41,467 --> 00:52:43,867
No, you're gonna make a
codpiece out of me.

1306
00:52:44,867 --> 00:52:47,500
I said in the head,
not the face.

1307
00:52:53,167 --> 00:52:54,867
I'm hungry, what you
got over there?

1308
00:52:54,900 --> 00:52:56,467
What's for dinner?

1309
00:53:05,367 --> 00:53:07,433
(humming)

1310
00:53:07,467 --> 00:53:08,533
Hey, hey!

1311
00:53:09,667 --> 00:53:12,000
Cross your legs, Robert, you
can see the squirrel.

1312
00:53:15,967 --> 00:53:18,467
I wanna go home with
that armadillo.

1313
00:53:25,733 --> 00:53:27,633
Hey buddy, you want an apple?

1314
00:53:27,667 --> 00:53:28,933
(laughs) I kid.

1315
00:53:30,733 --> 00:53:32,700
Say, you got a match, Robert?

1316
00:53:32,733 --> 00:53:33,867
Yeah.

1317
00:53:33,900 --> 00:53:35,733
William Shatner and
Robert Vaughan.

1318
00:53:35,767 --> 00:53:38,500
Lookit, he does got–
He has matches.

1319
00:53:38,533 --> 00:53:39,767
Unbelievable.

1320
00:53:42,400 --> 00:53:44,133
I hope they don't see me.

1321
00:53:44,167 --> 00:53:46,767
I could get in big trouble, this
is a national park.

1322
00:53:48,167 --> 00:53:50,600
(blowing air)

1323
00:53:57,767 --> 00:53:59,733
I am powerless over pyromania

1324
00:53:59,767 --> 00:54:02,500
and my life has become
unmanageable.

1325
00:54:05,933 --> 00:54:10,433
I ate it with Fava beans and a
nice Chianti. (slurping)

1326
00:54:10,467 --> 00:54:11,767
Wait a minute, don't eat it,

1327
00:54:11,800 --> 00:54:14,733
Corman wants to use that for a
monster in his next movie.

1328
00:54:14,767 --> 00:54:16,700
Hey, you think that fire's
big enough, Bob?

1329
00:54:16,733 --> 00:54:17,700
Whoa.

1330
00:54:25,167 --> 00:54:27,133
(laughing)

1331
00:54:27,167 --> 00:54:30,467
He looks like H.R. Pufnstuf
after a fiery car wreck.

1332
00:54:30,500 --> 00:54:33,200
Something goofy this way comes.

1333
00:54:34,467 --> 00:54:35,567
It's me!

1334
00:54:36,067 --> 00:54:37,633
I'm Trumpy!

1335
00:54:37,667 --> 00:54:38,700
Oh yeah.

1336
00:54:43,567 --> 00:54:46,000
Oh that's okay, don't say hi.

1337
00:54:48,567 --> 00:54:51,900
I hate to eat and run, but
(laughs) goodbye.

1338
00:54:51,933 --> 00:54:54,067
Bob, Bob, Bob of the Jungle,

1339
00:54:54,100 --> 00:54:55,733
friend to you and me.

1340
00:54:57,967 --> 00:55:00,167
Watch out for that tree.

1341
00:55:00,200 --> 00:55:01,467
I guess so.

1342
00:55:04,667 --> 00:55:06,533
The blood is clean.

1343
00:55:06,567 --> 00:55:08,633
Hyman Roth?

1344
00:55:09,500 --> 00:55:11,233
What the heck is he
talking about?

1345
00:55:11,267 --> 00:55:12,300
No clue.

1346
00:55:12,333 --> 00:55:13,800
He asks after his son.

1347
00:55:15,867 --> 00:55:18,867
Oh, he just had a Sealy
Posturpedic morning.

1348
00:55:18,900 --> 00:55:19,767
Yeah!

1349
00:55:20,767 --> 00:55:21,633
The boy.

1350
00:55:21,667 --> 00:55:23,533
I'm mad about the boy.

1351
00:55:23,567 --> 00:55:25,133
Bring him.

1352
00:55:26,067 --> 00:55:27,767
He is not here.

1353
00:55:27,800 --> 00:55:29,367
Where then?

1354
00:55:29,400 --> 00:55:30,733
Beyond the river.

1355
00:55:30,767 --> 00:55:34,733
And through the woods, to
grandmother's house he went.

1356
00:55:34,767 --> 00:55:35,967
A time ago.

1357
00:55:36,000 --> 00:55:37,967
How long is he gone?

1358
00:55:38,000 --> 00:55:41,233
Uh, a fireball and
two stones ago.

1359
00:55:41,267 --> 00:55:43,367
Two risings of the sun.

1360
00:55:43,400 --> 00:55:44,867
A couple of days, then.

1361
00:55:44,900 --> 00:55:46,033
Who knows of this?

1362
00:55:46,067 --> 00:55:47,233
All the clan.

1363
00:55:47,267 --> 00:55:48,500
He took others with him.

1364
00:55:48,533 --> 00:55:50,900
They're all talking about it.

1365
00:55:52,933 --> 00:55:54,433
Aw, if it's not one
thing it's another

1366
00:55:54,467 --> 00:55:56,133
around this crazy tribe.

1367
00:55:56,167 --> 00:55:59,933
(grunts) Oh boy, chili
peppers burn my gut.

1368
00:55:59,967 --> 00:56:02,300
Gotta go see a man about a dog.

1369
00:56:11,600 --> 00:56:13,467
Your son has broken the law.

1370
00:56:13,500 --> 00:56:14,800
He is beyond the river.

1371
00:56:14,833 --> 00:56:17,267
And he's totally off script!

1372
00:56:17,300 --> 00:56:20,133
Your blood will bring the
death to visit us!

1373
00:56:20,167 --> 00:56:22,367
As it was told in times past.

1374
00:56:22,400 --> 00:56:23,567
In the People column.

1375
00:56:23,600 --> 00:56:24,667
Boy.

1376
00:56:24,700 --> 00:56:26,867
Boy, crazy boy!

1377
00:56:27,467 --> 00:56:28,467
Tell me.

1378
00:56:28,500 --> 00:56:31,033
Your son led us to go
beyond the river.

1379
00:56:31,067 --> 00:56:33,067
We saw terrible things.

1380
00:56:33,100 --> 00:56:34,800
Great beasts fighting.

1381
00:56:34,833 --> 00:56:36,033
F Troop reruns.

1382
00:56:36,067 --> 00:56:37,467
One of us was taken
by the earth.

1383
00:56:37,500 --> 00:56:38,567
Which one?

1384
00:56:38,600 --> 00:56:40,467
- Lumpy, Mr. Cleaver. - A
fair-haired boy.

1385
00:56:40,500 --> 00:56:41,633
And my son?

1386
00:56:41,667 --> 00:56:43,433
We left him there.

1387
00:56:44,433 --> 00:56:45,400
Left him?

1388
00:56:45,433 --> 00:56:47,433
He didn't follow us back.

1389
00:56:47,467 --> 00:56:48,567
He's dead.

1390
00:56:48,600 --> 00:56:51,600
But the evil will come
all the same.

1391
00:56:51,633 --> 00:56:54,667
He's brought it down upon us.

1392
00:56:54,700 --> 00:56:55,767
No!

1393
00:56:55,800 --> 00:56:58,567
I will find him, bring him back!

1394
00:56:58,600 --> 00:57:01,000
I will leave no stone unturned,

1395
00:57:01,033 --> 00:57:04,633
starting with this one, yeah.

1396
00:57:04,667 --> 00:57:07,967
Wait, this is no time to
make flapjacks!

1397
00:57:08,000 --> 00:57:10,500
Okay, I want you to go deep.

1398
00:57:12,367 --> 00:57:13,567
Hm?

1399
00:57:13,600 --> 00:57:15,567
Run around in a circle.

1400
00:57:15,600 --> 00:57:17,267
At the sun's third rising.

1401
00:57:17,300 --> 00:57:19,467
We'll call it Wednesday,
about noon.

1402
00:57:19,500 --> 00:57:20,467
Nice.

1403
00:57:24,367 --> 00:57:26,433
Elias, Mr. Waverly!

1404
00:57:26,467 --> 00:57:27,400
Thrush.

1405
00:57:30,800 --> 00:57:33,267
Hey, he invented the hangover.

1406
00:57:34,767 --> 00:57:37,367
(vomiting noises)

1407
00:57:41,267 --> 00:57:44,967
I think that I will never see a
poem as lovely as, ow!

1408
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:50,000
(laughing dumbly)

1409
00:57:53,200 --> 00:57:55,033
Branch is funny.

1410
00:58:01,800 --> 00:58:05,200
I'm just a morning person,
what can I say?

1411
00:58:07,767 --> 00:58:10,400
Oh, he's inventing the violin.

1412
00:58:12,033 --> 00:58:13,433
Or the loom.

1413
00:58:17,467 --> 00:58:20,600
Gotta figure a way to pluck
these eyebrows.

1414
00:58:25,567 --> 00:58:26,867
Oh, come on.

1415
00:58:27,967 --> 00:58:30,400
Oh, wait, no, come on, let me
get this straight.

1416
00:58:30,433 --> 00:58:33,733
He got hit on the tree, and he
got smart, right?

1417
00:58:33,767 --> 00:58:34,967
Yep.

1418
00:58:35,000 --> 00:58:36,233
Uh huh.

1419
00:58:37,667 --> 00:58:38,467
Hm.

1420
00:58:39,767 --> 00:58:44,433
And it's a good thing for me, I
have my trusty dental floss!

1421
00:58:44,467 --> 00:58:47,400
Why I'm not sure, but I think
I've found the beginnings

1422
00:58:47,433 --> 00:58:49,267
of an Olympic event!

1423
00:58:55,567 --> 00:58:58,700
(humming)

1424
00:58:59,167 --> 00:59:00,567
Oh, petting zoo.

1425
00:59:00,600 --> 00:59:02,033
That seems nice.

1426
00:59:02,067 --> 00:59:03,733
Yeah, sweet.

1427
00:59:03,767 --> 00:59:05,567
You will die, doe.

1428
00:59:06,200 --> 00:59:07,833
Ross all over again.

1429
00:59:08,900 --> 00:59:11,367
So anyways, as I was saying,
there are three...

1430
00:59:11,400 --> 00:59:15,467
(dramatic music)

1431
00:59:17,000 --> 00:59:18,800
Honey, that was swell.

1432
00:59:18,833 --> 00:59:20,467
Well, see you later, dear.

1433
00:59:20,500 --> 00:59:23,300
I'm gonna go play Mahjong with
Betty and Frieda.

1434
00:59:25,767 --> 00:59:28,200
Don't you guys ever sleep?

1435
00:59:31,633 --> 00:59:34,400
Hey, he invented the mink stole!

1436
00:59:34,433 --> 00:59:35,600
That's a stiff deer.

1437
00:59:35,633 --> 00:59:36,800
Deerskin jacket.

1438
00:59:37,700 --> 00:59:41,567
Uh oh, Rob, your dad
found your stash!

1439
00:59:41,600 --> 00:59:43,200
Look at all of it!

1440
00:59:49,067 --> 00:59:52,533
Uh oh, they're on a collision
course for wackiness,

1441
00:59:52,567 --> 00:59:56,400
when Junior meets dad it's all
mixed up! (laughs goofily)

1442
00:59:59,400 --> 01:00:01,267
Marmaduke, no!

1443
01:00:01,300 --> 01:00:02,667
Wait, how can there
be Great Danes

1444
01:00:02,700 --> 01:00:05,000
when there isn't even
a Denmark yet?

1445
01:00:17,433 --> 01:00:20,700
That's a nice Chicago Cutlery
knife he's sporting there.

1446
01:00:22,367 --> 01:00:25,567
Bingo, Benji, Tramp, and Toto.

1447
01:00:26,600 --> 01:00:27,833
Toto too?

1448
01:00:27,867 --> 01:00:29,067
Uh huh.

1449
01:00:33,500 --> 01:00:35,667
Did he steal that from
an elk's lodge?

1450
01:00:37,500 --> 01:00:40,667
Oh here, take the deer, I gotta
see a man about a...

1451
01:00:40,700 --> 01:00:43,133
(barking)

1452
01:00:43,167 --> 01:00:45,567
Wait a minute, this is fake,
the deer's fake!

1453
01:00:45,600 --> 01:00:47,400
Get that guy, after him!

1454
01:00:55,100 --> 01:00:56,233
Ah, man bites dog.

1455
01:00:56,267 --> 01:00:58,000
I read about this in the paper.

1456
01:01:00,400 --> 01:01:01,233
Ooh!

1457
01:01:01,267 --> 01:01:03,000
All dogs go to heaven.

1458
01:01:03,033 --> 01:01:04,667
Bowser, no!

1459
01:01:05,600 --> 01:01:07,467
Come here, you, your
mother is furious.

1460
01:01:07,500 --> 01:01:08,767
But I was evolving, Dad!

1461
01:01:08,800 --> 01:01:10,000
Shut up, shut up,
we're going home.

1462
01:01:10,033 --> 01:01:11,533
Wait until your ancestors get.

1463
01:01:11,567 --> 01:01:12,467
We live by the word.

1464
01:01:12,500 --> 01:01:13,633
Grease is the word.

1465
01:01:13,667 --> 01:01:14,833
We die without it.

1466
01:01:14,867 --> 01:01:16,433
Oh, he's a
Precambrian evangelist.

1467
01:01:16,467 --> 01:01:17,667
Mhm.

1468
01:01:17,700 --> 01:01:19,367
It is told that the
breaker of the law

1469
01:01:19,400 --> 01:01:21,333
must be put to death.

1470
01:01:21,367 --> 01:01:22,633
Doodly doodly doo!

1471
01:01:22,667 --> 01:01:23,833
Wow, a swish pan!

1472
01:01:23,867 --> 01:01:25,200
They can use that later in
Man From Uncle!

1473
01:01:26,833 --> 01:01:29,800
Evil gods will come
down to kill!

1474
01:01:29,833 --> 01:01:31,433
As in times past.

1475
01:01:31,467 --> 01:01:33,733
Notice how I punched up the
word kill there?

1476
01:01:33,767 --> 01:01:35,000
That was my idea.

1477
01:01:35,033 --> 01:01:36,567
The keeper of the law
knows this is truth.

1478
01:01:36,600 --> 01:01:38,767
(snoring)

1479
01:01:38,800 --> 01:01:40,000
Wake up.

1480
01:01:40,033 --> 01:01:42,400
The son of the symbol
maker must die.

1481
01:01:42,433 --> 01:01:45,533
Hey, couldn't he just do some
community service instead?

1482
01:01:45,567 --> 01:01:46,800
(people shouting)

1483
01:01:46,833 --> 01:01:48,333
Hey!

1484
01:01:48,367 --> 01:01:49,800
Hey I don't know, it's new, I
just thought of it.

1485
01:01:49,833 --> 01:01:51,200
Hey?

1486
01:01:51,233 --> 01:01:52,967
Each of us have wandered
after the truth.

1487
01:01:53,000 --> 01:01:55,467
The word tells us that
the law is truth.

1488
01:01:55,500 --> 01:01:56,767
Mhm.

1489
01:01:56,800 --> 01:01:58,833
- This one has broken the law. -
The word or the law?

1490
01:01:58,867 --> 01:02:00,767
But still the gods have not come

1491
01:02:00,800 --> 01:02:03,200
as it's told they will come.

1492
01:02:03,233 --> 01:02:05,667
Door number one! Take
the curtain!

1493
01:02:05,700 --> 01:02:06,967
Evil's near us.

1494
01:02:07,000 --> 01:02:09,767
The clan will be no more.

1495
01:02:09,800 --> 01:02:13,733
I say only to wait
until it does come.

1496
01:02:13,767 --> 01:02:16,033
And I say it must be kept
from the people

1497
01:02:16,067 --> 01:02:17,533
by another death!

1498
01:02:17,567 --> 01:02:18,433
Ooh.

1499
01:02:18,467 --> 01:02:20,833
The word of the law is truth.

1500
01:02:20,867 --> 01:02:25,667
Let the guilty one be as
dead until manhood.

1501
01:02:25,700 --> 01:02:28,333
Gee, it's kind of like
Inherit the Wind.

1502
01:02:28,367 --> 01:02:29,733
Only backwards.

1503
01:02:29,767 --> 01:02:30,933
No, no!

1504
01:02:30,967 --> 01:02:34,333
♪ No no, no no no no,
no no no no

1505
01:02:34,367 --> 01:02:35,633
(laughs)

1506
01:02:35,667 --> 01:02:39,000
It shall be as the
symbol maker says!

1507
01:02:39,033 --> 01:02:40,867
Hey, don't I get an appeal?

1508
01:02:43,767 --> 01:02:45,967
(chuckles) An amateur
photographer caught this footage

1509
01:02:46,000 --> 01:02:47,500
of early policeman.

1510
01:02:49,600 --> 01:02:51,333
(muffled cries)

1511
01:02:51,367 --> 01:02:53,533
Stop it, Dad, uncle Bob is
picking on me again!

1512
01:02:53,567 --> 01:02:55,767
(muffled groans)

1513
01:02:56,633 --> 01:02:58,200
Oh, this must be

1514
01:02:58,233 --> 01:03:01,367
where professional
wrestling got its start.

1515
01:03:06,267 --> 01:03:09,767
Ah right, like you had good luck
with that thing before.

1516
01:03:17,067 --> 01:03:20,567
Why couldn't I just get
cast in Daddy-O?

1517
01:03:20,600 --> 01:03:25,567
(humming over dramatic music)

1518
01:03:32,100 --> 01:03:32,967
Enough!

1519
01:03:33,567 --> 01:03:37,500
(fun futuristic music)

1520
01:03:41,200 --> 01:03:42,100
Hm?

1521
01:03:43,467 --> 01:03:46,900
Oh, sorry everybody, I'm sorry.

1522
01:03:47,767 --> 01:03:48,900
What?

1523
01:03:49,800 --> 01:03:52,033
What did I do? He started it!

1524
01:03:53,033 --> 01:03:54,767
All right folks, show's over,

1525
01:03:54,800 --> 01:03:57,633
nothing to see here,
everybody go home.

1526
01:03:57,667 --> 01:03:58,733
We should have left early.

1527
01:03:58,767 --> 01:04:00,500
Now there's gonna be
a traffic jam.

1528
01:04:05,967 --> 01:04:08,600
Oh, suddenly I'm the jerk.

1529
01:04:12,100 --> 01:04:13,467
Poor sap.

1530
01:04:15,767 --> 01:04:17,000
(sweet music)

1531
01:04:17,033 --> 01:04:17,733
Oh, hey.

1532
01:04:17,767 --> 01:04:19,067
Esther Williams.

1533
01:04:19,900 --> 01:04:23,033
Now wait a minute,
she's got buttons?

1534
01:04:23,067 --> 01:04:25,600
No word for day, but
she's got buttons.

1535
01:04:25,633 --> 01:04:26,767
Terrific.

1536
01:04:28,233 --> 01:04:29,067
Say.

1537
01:04:29,800 --> 01:04:31,733
Hey, he's playing a Fudgicle!

1538
01:04:31,767 --> 01:04:32,767
Fudgsicle.

1539
01:04:32,800 --> 01:04:34,433
I always called it Fudgicle.

1540
01:04:35,300 --> 01:04:36,533
Sounds like the theme song

1541
01:04:36,567 --> 01:04:38,767
from Please Don't Eat
the Daisies.

1542
01:04:42,700 --> 01:04:45,067
He's gonna eat it later,
it's made of wax.

1543
01:04:45,100 --> 01:04:46,633
You dropped your soap! (laughs)

1544
01:04:46,667 --> 01:04:47,967
Just kidding.

1545
01:04:50,367 --> 01:04:51,600
Say.

1546
01:04:54,300 --> 01:04:56,733
I know you're not to give voice
to me or I to you.

1547
01:04:56,767 --> 01:04:58,800
But I can stand here and
watch you, right?

1548
01:04:58,833 --> 01:05:00,967
Listen to this voice, then.

1549
01:05:01,700 --> 01:05:04,733
(blows flute)

1550
01:05:04,767 --> 01:05:08,000
Oh, I Talked To the Wind
by King Crimson!

1551
01:05:12,300 --> 01:05:15,600
Actually, I call this one
Opus One, Number One.

1552
01:05:23,767 --> 01:05:26,267
Um, like, do you know any Tull?

1553
01:05:29,233 --> 01:05:31,400
That voice I've heard at night.

1554
01:05:31,433 --> 01:05:32,967
In the life of dreams.

1555
01:05:33,000 --> 01:05:35,400
His skirt's shorter than hers.

1556
01:05:35,433 --> 01:05:37,533
I came to find it
beyond the river.

1557
01:05:37,567 --> 01:05:40,000
It is not a bad place that gives
the voice of dreams.

1558
01:05:40,033 --> 01:05:42,633
What are you, Carl Jung
all of a sudden?

1559
01:05:42,667 --> 01:05:45,233
There are strange things.

1560
01:05:45,267 --> 01:05:49,367
So I wonder how many strange
