01:16:35,500 --> 01:16:36,833
Don't think so.

1820
01:16:36,867 --> 01:16:38,500
We could make a place
to lie down on.

1821
01:16:38,533 --> 01:16:40,200
Oh, wow. (claps)

1822
01:16:40,233 --> 01:16:42,833
So the cold couldn't reach
us as we slept.

1823
01:16:42,867 --> 01:16:44,967
We'll be a modern
Stone Age family.

1824
01:16:46,633 --> 01:16:47,700
Aye.

1825
01:16:48,333 --> 01:16:50,067
When will you start?

1826
01:16:50,100 --> 01:16:51,333
Next semester.

1827
01:16:52,167 --> 01:16:53,333
No.

1828
01:16:55,067 --> 01:16:57,133
Beyond the river, there
are warm skins

1829
01:16:57,167 --> 01:16:58,700
of so many animals.

1830
01:16:58,733 --> 01:17:02,000
And we can stuff the skin with
cheese and bacon bits.

1831
01:17:02,033 --> 01:17:03,533
And there are growing
things there

1832
01:17:03,567 --> 01:17:06,067
that are softer to lie on.

1833
01:17:06,100 --> 01:17:09,133
And the place smells of wind
and fresh things.

1834
01:17:09,167 --> 01:17:10,467
Like donuts?

1835
01:17:13,833 --> 01:17:15,333
You must stay here.

1836
01:17:16,500 --> 01:17:19,200
So make a sleeping place for
us on the high path.

1837
01:17:19,233 --> 01:17:21,933
I think you're wonderful,
you know that?

1838
01:17:25,433 --> 01:17:27,167
(yawns)

1839
01:17:27,967 --> 01:17:29,167
Fore!

1840
01:17:33,333 --> 01:17:34,667
What does he do?

1841
01:17:34,700 --> 01:17:36,133
He's a consultant!

1842
01:17:36,167 --> 01:17:38,067
He makes a sleeping place for
him and his woman!

1843
01:17:38,100 --> 01:17:39,200
Why?

1844
01:17:39,233 --> 01:17:40,600
Have you seen the woman?

1845
01:17:40,633 --> 01:17:42,033
Ooh!

1846
01:17:42,067 --> 01:17:45,167
There is no word of
law against it.

1847
01:17:46,633 --> 01:17:47,433
Fool.

1848
01:17:47,933 --> 01:17:49,767
Fool on the hill.

1849
01:17:51,033 --> 01:17:53,333
Hey, he's doing a
centerfold for GQ.

1850
01:17:53,367 --> 01:17:55,100
Grog Quarterly.

1851
01:18:00,167 --> 01:18:03,233
So, how many
toasters did we get?

1852
01:18:03,267 --> 01:18:04,100
Aye.

1853
01:18:05,833 --> 01:18:07,100
Whoa.

1854
01:18:07,133 --> 01:18:09,733
You kept me at this sleeping
place a long, long time.

1855
01:18:09,767 --> 01:18:10,733
Aye.

1856
01:18:11,100 --> 01:18:12,067
Aye.

1857
01:18:12,633 --> 01:18:14,233
But I wonder still.

1858
01:18:14,267 --> 01:18:16,100
Someone must break the law.

1859
01:18:16,133 --> 01:18:17,667
Oh, shut up!

1860
01:18:17,700 --> 01:18:19,133
Must find the truth.

1861
01:18:19,167 --> 01:18:20,200
For all and forever.

1862
01:18:20,233 --> 01:18:22,300
Always and forever?

1863
01:18:22,333 --> 01:18:25,800
Of all things, the clan
fears the god

1864
01:18:25,833 --> 01:18:28,700
that brings death with its
touch the most.

1865
01:18:28,733 --> 01:18:29,600
Hm.

1866
01:18:30,333 --> 01:18:33,100
I'll find it, and kill it.

1867
01:18:33,133 --> 01:18:34,333
For 10.

1868
01:18:37,133 --> 01:18:39,100
Get me some food.

1869
01:18:39,133 --> 01:18:40,100
Now.

1870
01:18:40,133 --> 01:18:42,133
And a beer, now.

1871
01:18:42,167 --> 01:18:43,633
Do as I say.

1872
01:18:43,667 --> 01:18:44,900
Not as I do.

1873
01:18:44,933 --> 01:18:47,533
I hear you in all things,
but not in this.

1874
01:18:47,567 --> 01:18:50,400
Why should you be the one
to break the law?

1875
01:18:50,433 --> 01:18:53,133
Every man holds to the old
laws the safe way.

1876
01:18:53,167 --> 01:18:54,500
(snoring)

1877
01:18:54,533 --> 01:18:56,933
This script's like a
telephone directory!

1878
01:18:56,967 --> 01:18:58,500
Only not as interesting.

1879
01:18:58,533 --> 01:19:01,100
No one wants to take the risks
that a better life demands.

1880
01:19:01,133 --> 01:19:02,800
And the law is the word and
the word is the law,

1881
01:19:02,833 --> 01:19:04,067
we know!

1882
01:19:05,467 --> 01:19:08,100
So the ages pass and the
clan remains huddled

1883
01:19:08,133 --> 01:19:09,233
in the same place.

1884
01:19:09,267 --> 01:19:11,100
In spite of rent control!

1885
01:19:11,133 --> 01:19:12,733
There's no more to say.

1886
01:19:12,767 --> 01:19:14,700
It is time to act.

1887
01:19:14,733 --> 01:19:17,067
This is why the
dinosaurs died out.

1888
01:19:17,100 --> 01:19:19,167
You bored them to death!

1889
01:19:21,133 --> 01:19:22,967
I'll go towel off.

1890
01:19:27,167 --> 01:19:29,900
Oh neat, he invented the quiver.

1891
01:19:29,933 --> 01:19:31,300
Ooh, so did she!

1892
01:19:31,333 --> 01:19:32,433
Ooh!

1893
01:19:32,467 --> 01:19:33,633
Sorry.

1894
01:19:37,133 --> 01:19:39,533
Hold me, you big galoot!

1895
01:19:39,567 --> 01:19:40,833
Wanna be alone?

1896
01:19:40,867 --> 01:19:42,900
Not here, no.

1897
01:19:47,167 --> 01:19:50,967
Remember to assert yourself at
work, you're the best!

1898
01:19:53,167 --> 01:19:54,233
I love you!

1899
01:19:54,267 --> 01:19:55,933
Come on, you can say it!

1900
01:19:55,967 --> 01:19:56,933
Come on.

1901
01:19:56,967 --> 01:19:59,067
Oh, I love you too.

1902
