2087
01:28:55,767 --> 01:28:57,567
Wait, what's this?

2088
01:29:00,700 --> 01:29:02,767
It's a vintage contemporary!

2089
01:29:03,633 --> 01:29:05,667
It bears a symbol.

2090
01:29:05,700 --> 01:29:07,600
Bright lights, big cave.

2091
01:29:10,100 --> 01:29:12,333
This must be the way man
should greet man.

2092
01:29:12,367 --> 01:29:13,667
Formal and rigid.

2093
01:29:13,700 --> 01:29:15,733
- His hands without a weapon.
- Oh, come on.

2094
01:29:21,933 --> 01:29:22,800
Hm.

2095
01:29:22,833 --> 01:29:24,100
What symbols are these?

2096
01:29:24,133 --> 01:29:25,667
That's right, by Uncle
headquarters!

2097
01:29:25,700 --> 01:29:28,133
I have none like
these in my mind.

2098
01:29:28,167 --> 01:29:30,600
And these were made in a
way unknown to me.

2099
01:29:30,633 --> 01:29:32,367
Yeah, at the Photomat.

2100
01:29:32,400 --> 01:29:33,633
All of this.

2101
01:29:34,900 --> 01:29:36,933
Are these symbols too?

2102
01:29:36,967 --> 01:29:38,167
Perhaps.

2103
01:29:38,600 --> 01:29:39,633
Maybe.

2104
01:29:40,433 --> 01:29:42,367
Someday they must be known.

2105
01:29:44,300 --> 01:29:46,067
It is a thing of wonder.

2106
01:29:46,100 --> 01:29:49,100
Yeah, I wonder when the
film's gonna end.

2107
01:29:51,733 --> 01:29:54,700
Shall we take him to the cave
and make a cairn for him?

2108
01:29:54,733 --> 01:29:56,267
Nah, let's eat 'em here.

2109
01:29:56,300 --> 01:29:58,200
Leave them in this
place that was his.

2110
01:29:58,233 --> 01:30:01,167
The people have seen, a
new law is made.

2111
01:30:01,200 --> 01:30:04,300
Food will be gathered,
wheel things made,

2112
01:30:04,333 --> 01:30:07,733
and the clan will seek out other
men in other places.

2113
01:30:07,767 --> 01:30:09,667
Other voices, other rooms.

2114
01:30:09,700 --> 01:30:10,633
We'll take this thing of wonder.

2115
01:30:11,733 --> 01:30:14,700
Somewhere a man may be able to
tell us the words.

2116
01:30:14,733 --> 01:30:15,800
Hey, Bob!

2117
01:30:15,833 --> 01:30:17,267
Bob, wake up, Bob.

2118
01:30:17,300 --> 01:30:18,400
There.

2119
01:30:18,433 --> 01:30:19,967
Or one of us may find
a way to know.

2120
01:30:20,000 --> 01:30:21,933
I bet his initials are
Robert Vaughn.

2121
01:30:21,967 --> 01:30:22,900
Aye.

2122
01:30:24,133 --> 01:30:25,967
So let this man stay.

2123
01:30:26,000 --> 01:30:28,333
He will not be alone.

2124
01:30:30,500 --> 01:30:33,567
Well, this guy's getting ripe,
let's get out of here.

2125
01:30:37,967 --> 01:30:39,033
So, bye.

2126
01:30:41,800 --> 01:30:43,167
Hey I just thought of something.

2127
01:30:43,200 --> 01:30:45,600
Who's gonna play the
Indian on F Troop?

2128
01:30:46,567 --> 01:30:48,967
(Man): I and a party
of 23 others...

2129
01:30:49,000 --> 01:30:50,100
What?

2130
01:30:50,133 --> 01:30:51,600
...were on a
scientific expedition

2131
01:30:51,633 --> 01:30:53,300
when the bombs began to fall.

2132
01:30:53,333 --> 01:30:54,867
- Oh. - Oh, message!

2133
01:30:54,900 --> 01:30:56,533
Message coming in, people.

2134
01:30:56,567 --> 01:30:58,300
I think it's from
Beach Dickerson.

2135
01:30:58,333 --> 01:31:00,267
...was unleashed all
over the world.

2136
01:31:00,300 --> 01:31:02,600
Retaliation added to
retaliation.

2137
01:31:02,633 --> 01:31:04,500
Oh, I see a president's face.

2138
01:31:04,533 --> 01:31:07,700
Until all traces of man's
works had been wiped

2139
01:31:07,733 --> 01:31:08,933
from the face of the Earth.

2140
01:31:08,967 --> 01:31:10,333
Sorry everyone, sorry.

2141
01:31:10,367 --> 01:31:11,667
I'm hot, I'm on fire.

2142
01:31:11,700 --> 01:31:14,100
(clicking noises)

2143
01:31:14,133 --> 01:31:17,500
Some grew huge
beyond all reason

2144
01:31:17,533 --> 01:31:20,000
and formed as the
dinosaurs of prehistory,

2145
01:31:20,033 --> 01:31:22,400
or took on new
shapes altogether,

2146
01:31:22,433 --> 01:31:24,100
mad in shape and purpose.

2147
01:31:24,133 --> 01:31:26,333
They became stock footage.

2148
01:31:26,367 --> 01:31:27,600
My comrades and I,
half-protected

2149
01:31:27,633 --> 01:31:31,300
by our radiation suits, found
ourselves given an age

2150
01:31:31,333 --> 01:31:33,700
far beyond the span allowed.

2151
01:31:33,733 --> 01:31:34,700
Hm.

2152
01:31:34,733 --> 01:31:36,533
Out of all the
sprawling millions

2153
01:31:36,567 --> 01:31:39,600
of the Earth a handful
escaped all harm

2154
01:31:39,633 --> 01:31:41,900
through fortune or design.

2155
01:31:41,933 --> 01:31:43,467
Oh, kinda like Neil Bush.

2156
01:31:43,500 --> 01:31:45,933
After the holocaust, the
wisest of them

2157
01:31:45,967 --> 01:31:48,667
set down a long list of taboos.

2158
01:31:48,700 --> 01:31:50,200
Am I the wisest?

2159
01:31:50,233 --> 01:31:51,567
Yeah, I'm the wisest.

2160
01:31:51,600 --> 01:31:52,867
Pretty much.

2161
01:31:52,900 --> 01:31:54,700
The laws are in the form of
a religion now.

2162
01:31:54,733 --> 01:31:58,367
It's strange to see them living
the life of Cro-Magnon man.

2163
01:31:58,400 --> 01:32:00,533
Cro-Magnon, P.I.

2164
01:32:01,567 --> 01:32:04,267
On occasion we tried to
contact them,

2165
01:32:04,300 --> 01:32:06,133
but they feared us.

2166
01:32:06,767 --> 01:32:07,967
Wonder why.

2167
01:32:08,000 --> 01:32:09,200
And our radiation killed those

2168
01:32:09,233 --> 01:32:10,600
who came too close.

2169
01:32:10,633 --> 01:32:12,600
Now, only I'm left,

2170
01:32:12,633 --> 01:32:17,400
and the radiation has worn away
these long, long years.

2171
01:32:17,433 --> 01:32:19,267
So you know it's okay.

2172
01:32:19,300 --> 01:32:21,533
Now a new one
thinks and wonders

2173
01:32:21,567 --> 01:32:23,133
about the truth of the law.

2174
01:32:23,167 --> 01:32:24,767
He's a real goosester!

2175
01:32:24,800 --> 01:32:27,267
Perhaps man will dare
to try again.

2176
01:32:27,300 --> 01:32:29,500
I am very lonely.

2177
01:32:29,533 --> 01:32:31,267
In fact, I'm dead.

2178
01:32:31,300 --> 01:32:33,267
Very, very tired.

2179
01:32:33,300 --> 01:32:34,700
Dead tired.

2180
01:32:35,733 --> 01:32:37,333
This happened a long time ago.

2181
01:32:37,367 --> 01:32:38,600
(humming)

2182
01:32:38,633 --> 01:32:41,467
And as you know, men did
meet other men.

2183
01:32:41,500 --> 01:32:44,400
And fire smelted metal,
made explosives.

2184
01:32:44,433 --> 01:32:47,767
The wheel turned machines and
made gun barrels.

2185
01:32:47,800 --> 01:32:51,000
The towers were built
and flattened.

2186
01:32:51,033 --> 01:32:53,400
How many times?

2187
01:32:53,433 --> 01:32:55,367
Will it happen again?

2188
01:32:56,600 --> 01:33:01,533
And if it does, will any at all
survive the next time?

2189
01:33:01,567 --> 01:33:03,733
Doubtful, let's go.

2190
01:33:03,767 --> 01:33:06,167
Or will it be the end?

2191
01:33:06,200 --> 01:33:07,200
Heavy.

2192
01:33:07,233 --> 01:33:08,467
Robert Vaughn will be back

2193
01:33:08,500 --> 01:33:10,300
in the Sweet Sweetback Affair!

2194
01:33:26,400 --> 01:33:28,333
Aye, I am the last survivor

2195
01:33:28,367 --> 01:33:30,367
of a movie-watching experiment!

2196
01:33:30,400 --> 01:33:31,467
Me too!

2197
01:33:31,500 --> 01:33:32,733
Oh yeah, him too!

2198
01:33:32,767 --> 01:33:33,967
Sh, character.

2199
01:33:34,000 --> 01:33:35,567
Whether through
fortune or design,

2200
01:33:35,600 --> 01:33:36,967
we are the only survivors.

2201
01:33:37,000 --> 01:33:39,500
The awesome power of Roger
Corman was unleashed

2202
01:33:39,533 --> 01:33:41,967
upon the satellite and
scared everybody!

2203
01:33:42,000 --> 01:33:44,200
it was brought upon us
by scientists

2204
01:33:44,233 --> 01:33:45,800
mad in shape and purpose.

2205
01:33:45,833 --> 01:33:47,133
Aye, aye.

2206
01:33:47,167 --> 01:33:48,533
And the fact that I am dead
does not prevent me

2207
01:33:48,567 --> 01:33:49,900
from tying up a few loose ends.

2208
01:33:49,933 --> 01:33:51,267
Me too, you keep
forgetting about me!

2209
01:33:51,300 --> 01:33:52,167
Oh yeah, him too.

2210
01:33:52,200 --> 01:33:52,800
Sh, character.

2211
01:33:52,833 --> 01:33:54,333
Aye!

2212
01:33:54,367 --> 01:33:56,167
I have, protected by our
Trumpy radiation suits,

2213
01:33:56,200 --> 01:33:57,533
wait for contact.

2214
01:33:57,567 --> 01:33:59,467
Hey, hi guys, what's up?

2215
01:33:59,500 --> 01:34:00,767
Human!

2216
01:34:00,800 --> 01:34:02,500
Oh, you guys, come on.

2217
01:34:02,533 --> 01:34:05,500
Aye, he was the young one
who began to wonder.

2218
01:34:05,533 --> 01:34:08,100
I'm starting to wonder
about these two.

2219
01:34:08,133 --> 01:34:10,900
He was unfettered by a long
list of taboos,

2220
01:34:10,933 --> 01:34:13,700
except that he refused to
wear silly hats.

2221
01:34:13,733 --> 01:34:15,567
Listen, are you guys
supposed to be dead?

2222
01:34:15,600 --> 01:34:17,133
You know, I can see
your lips move.

2223
01:34:17,167 --> 01:34:20,267
Aye, we refuse to ad lib and
give in to his demands

2224
01:34:20,300 --> 01:34:23,867
and smell his feet, which were
like bad meat or good cheese!

2225
01:34:23,900 --> 01:34:25,667
Oh come on you guys, quit
your clowning.

2226
01:34:25,700 --> 01:34:27,600
I'm supposed to read the letter,
okay?

2227
01:34:27,633 --> 01:34:29,800
One took great pleasure in
reading letters.

2228
01:34:29,833 --> 01:34:30,667
Aye.

2229
01:34:30,700 --> 01:34:31,567
Where is it?

2230
01:34:31,600 --> 01:34:32,667
It's supposed to be here.

2231
01:34:32,700 --> 01:34:34,367
Letter, letter! It's the the
radiation suits!

2232
01:34:34,400 --> 01:34:35,767
Letter, letter!

2233
01:34:35,800 --> 01:34:37,800
Oh, geez, come on!

2234
01:34:37,833 --> 01:34:39,667
Tickle the old ones.

2235
01:34:39,700 --> 01:34:41,667
Sorry about the slime,
young one.

2236
01:34:41,700 --> 01:34:45,300
It's covered in slime and this
matted monkey hair,

2237
01:34:45,333 --> 01:34:48,667
fake monkey hair that you made
these suits out of.

2238
01:34:48,700 --> 01:34:50,933
It comes with the territory,
young one.

2239
01:34:50,967 --> 01:34:56,400
Okay, well, let's put this
on still, Cambot.

2240
01:34:57,767 --> 01:34:58,900
You got that?

2241
01:34:58,933 --> 01:35:00,700
Well this is a pretty neat one,

2242
01:35:00,733 --> 01:35:01,967
before it got slimed.

2243
01:35:02,000 --> 01:35:05,167
It's from Bruce Barber,
and it says,

2244
01:35:05,200 --> 01:35:07,700
"Verify ye hence and
testify furthermore,

2245
01:35:07,733 --> 01:35:09,600
"that your show has a large
and loyal following

2246
01:35:09,633 --> 01:35:11,567
"among the professional
stuntmen here in L.A.

2247
01:35:11,600 --> 01:35:13,733
"Nothing brings home
to us exactly

2248
01:35:13,767 --> 01:35:15,800
"how far the stunt
business has come,

2249
01:35:15,833 --> 01:35:17,400
"as watching the action

2250
01:35:17,433 --> 01:35:20,167
"on some of the turkeys you
have graced us with.

2251
01:35:20,200 --> 01:35:21,667
"I try never to miss a show.

2252
01:35:21,700 --> 01:35:22,800
"The wife, who thinks
I'm sick...”

2253
01:35:22,833 --> 01:35:24,067
The wife?

2254
01:35:24,100 --> 01:35:25,200
- The wife? (chuckles) -
“...tapes them for me

2255
01:35:25,233 --> 01:35:26,567
"when I'm on location.

2256
01:35:26,600 --> 01:35:28,600
"Please keep up the good,
bad work."

2257
01:35:28,633 --> 01:35:29,800
Bruce Barber.

2258
01:35:29,833 --> 01:35:31,067
Pretty neat, huh?

2259
01:35:31,100 --> 01:35:32,600
Aye.

2260
01:35:32,633 --> 01:35:33,667
You guys are gonna have to clean
all this up, you know.

2261
01:35:33,700 --> 01:35:34,933
Again with the taboo.

2262
01:35:34,967 --> 01:35:36,200
Nay, nay!

2263
01:35:36,233 --> 01:35:38,200
Just be quiet, we gotta
get outta here.

2264
01:35:38,233 --> 01:35:40,000
What do you think, sirs?

2265
01:35:40,033 --> 01:35:42,733
Mm, that is good.

2266
01:35:43,900 --> 01:35:46,467
I'm glad I brought the
orange cappuccino.

2267
01:35:46,500 --> 01:35:49,600
Wait a minute, I brought the
orange cappuccino.

2268
01:35:49,633 --> 01:35:51,567
(laughing)

2269
01:35:51,600 --> 01:35:52,933
(wincing)

2270
01:35:54,733 --> 01:35:57,400
Oh, hello bubbie, Frank and I
are just patching things up

2271
01:35:57,433 --> 01:35:59,533
with a little cup of kindness.

2272
01:36:02,567 --> 01:36:03,767
You know, it's the quiet moments

2273
01:36:03,800 --> 01:36:05,767
that are the most
precious moments.

2274
01:36:05,800 --> 01:36:07,000
Mm.

2275
01:36:07,033 --> 01:36:08,800
Why don't you push the button,
Frank?

2276
01:36:08,833 --> 01:36:12,333
I'm going to slip this tape of
Dad in with Jack Lemmon.

2277
01:36:12,367 --> 01:36:15,533
I think we could both use a
good cry, don't you?

2278
01:36:15,567 --> 01:36:17,233
I'll make some popcorn.

2279
01:36:21,533 --> 01:36:23,300
(laughing)

2280
01:36:23,333 --> 01:36:26,033
(pained groans)

2281
01:36:29,167 --> 01:36:33,200
(majestic music)

